## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design production-grade canaries with data-plane shadowing and multi-service integrations using Google-native tooling.

## Key Concepts
- Canary deployments with per-revision traffic
- Shadow traffic for data validation
- Pub/Sub driven sinks to BigQuery
- Cloud Monitoring alert policies and auto rollback
- Least-privilege IAM

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: emit prod request and publish shadow copy
async function handle(req){
  const prodResp = await prodEndpoint(req);
  await publishShadow(copyRequest(req));
  return prodResp;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure idempotency and avoid double writes if shadow sink duplicates fail?
- How to test rollback safety and prevent drift between prod and shadow data?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses real-world skills in GitOps, policy-as-code, cross-region DR, and automated rollback.

## Key Concepts
- GitOps and Cloud Deploy
- Policy-as-code with OPA
- CMEK and IAM Conditions
- Canary traffic routing across GKE/Cloud Run
- Drift detection and regional failover

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: trigger a rollback if a metric breaches a threshold
async function maybeRollback(metrics) {
  if (metrics.latency > 500 || metrics.errorRate > 0.02) {
    await cloudDeploy.rollback();
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift detection across regions?
- How do you simulate regional outages and verify failover?
